## DESCRIPTION
## Algebra: Basic Algebra, Exponents and Radicals
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by cmd6a 4/4/06

## DBsubject(Algebra)
## DBchapter(Properties of exponents, rational exponents and radicals)
## DBsection(Properties of exponents)
## Date(6/3/2002)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('College Algebra')
## AuthorText1('Stewart, Redlin, Watson')
## EditionText1('3')
## Section1('1.3')
## Problem1('3')
## KEYWORDS('algebra')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl");

Context("LimitedNumeric");

$a = random(2, 4);
$b = random(2, 3);
$c = random(5, 6);
$d = random(2, 4);

$ans =
    Real($a**(-$b) * $c**$d)->with(tolerance => .00005, tolType => "absolute");

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the following expression:


     [``[$a] ^{-[$b] } [$c] ^{[$d]}\ ``] = [_]{$ans}{10}

Your answer must be a number not an algebraic expression.  Decimal numbers are OK if they are accurate to at least four decimal places, but fractions are preferable.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[``[$a] ^{-[$b] } [$c] ^{[$d]} = \frac{[$c] ^{[$d]}}{[$a] ^{[$b]}}  
 = \frac{[@ $c**$d @]}{[@ $a**$b @]} = [$ans] ``]  
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    
